<title>INDIA: AIG unit to invest in Indian drug firm.</title>
<headline>AIG unit to invest in Indian drug firm.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>American International Group (AIG) has entered into an agreement with India's Ciba CKD Biochem Ltd to invest $4.8 million in the company, the Indian firm said.</p>
<p>Ciba CKD is a joint venture of Ciba-Geigy of Switzerland and Chong Kun Dang of Korea. The firm is building a plant to manufacture 125 tonnes per year of anti-tuberculosis drug rifampicin at Mahad in western India.</p>
<p>The plant is expected to start operations in the second quarter of this year, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>AIG, in collaboration with India's Infrastructure Leasing and Services Ltd, is also in the process of setting up a AIG Indian Sectoral Equity Fund, which will invest in Indian infrastructure, it said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
